    DATED NOVEMBER 30, 2018 ON PENALTIES FOR ADMINISTRATIVE CIVIL AVIATION OFFENCES
   AMENDED BY THE GOVERNMENT’S DECREE NO. 123/2021/ND-CP DATED DECEMBER 28, 2021 ON
         AMENDMENTS TO SOME ARTICLES OF DECREES ON SEVERAL ARTICLES OF DECREES
     PROVIDING FOR PENALTIES FOR ADMINISTRATIVE MARITIME OFFENCES; ADMINISTRATIVE
    ROAD TRAFFIC OFFENCES AND RAIL TRANSPORT OFFENCES; CIVIL AVIATION OFFENCES AND
       GOVERNMENT’S DECREE NO. 282/2025/ND-CP DATED OCTOBER 30, 2025 PROVIDING FOR
      PENALTIES FOR ADMINISTRATIVE OFFENCES IN FIELDS OF SECURITY, SOCIAL ORDER AND
     SAFETY; SOCIAL VICE PREVENTION AND COMBAT; DOMESTIC VIOLENCE PREVENTION AND
        COMBAT REGARDING POWER TO IMPOSE PENALTIES FOR ADMINISTRATIVE OFFENCES

  Pursuant to the Law on Government Organization No. 63/2025/QH15;

  Pursuant to the Law on Handling of Administrative Violations No. 15/2012/QH13 amended by the Law No.
  54/2014/QH13, Law No. 18/2017/QH14, Law No. 67/2020/QH14, Law No. 09/2022/QH15, Law No.
  56/2024/QH15, Law No. 88/2025/QH15;

  Pursuant to the Law on Civil Aviation of Vietnam No. 66/2006/QH11 amended by the Law No. 61/2014/QH13;

  At the request of the Minister of Construction;

  The Government hereby promulgates a Decree on amendments to several Articles of the Government’s Decree
  No. 162/2018/ND-CP dated November 30, 2018 on penalties for administrative civil aviation offences amended
  by the Government’s Decree No. 123/2021/ND-CP dated December 28, 2021 on amendments to some Articles of
  Decrees on several articles of decrees providing for penalties for administrative maritime offences;
  administrative road traffic offences and rail transport offences; civil aviation offences and Government’s Decree
  No. 282/2025/ND-CP dated October 30, 2025 providing for penalties for administrative offences in fields of
  security, social order and safety; social vice prevention and combat; domestic violence prevention and combat
  (Decree No. 162/2018/ND-CP) regarding power to impose penalties for administrative offences.

  Article 1. Amendments to Article 31 of the Decree No. 162/2018/ND-CP

  “Article 31. Power to impose penalties of inspectors

  1. During the inspection period, inspectors of the Inspectorate of the Ministry of Public Security and Vietnam
  Aviation Inspectorate have the power to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 10,000,000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences if its value is not
  02 times as high as the penalty amount specified in point b of this clause.

  2. Chiefs of the Vietnam Aviation Inspectorate and Inspectorate of the Fire and Rescue Police Department and
  provincial Police Departments have the power to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 50,000,000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences;

  d) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.

  3. Chief Inspector of the Vietnam Aviation Inspectorate; Chief Inspector of the Inspectorate of the Fire and
  Rescue Police Department; Chief Inspectors of provincial Police Departments have the power to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 80,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.

  4. Chief Inspector of the Inspectorate of the Ministry of Public Security; head of the inspection team established
  by the Chief Inspector of the Inspectorate of the Ministry of Public Security have the power to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 100,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.”.

  Article 2. Article 31a is added after Article 31 of the Decree No. 162/2018/ND-CP

   “Article 31a. Power of heads of agencies performing state management tasks

  1. The Director General of the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam is entitled to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 100,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.

  2. During the examination period, the head of the examination team established by the Director General of the
  Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam is entitled to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 80,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.

  3. During the examination period, the head of the examination team established by the Minister of Construction
  and the Minister of Public Security is entitled to impose penalties for administrative offences as prescribed in
  clause 1 of this Article.”.

  Article 3. Amendments to Article 32 of the Decree No. 162/2018/ND-CP

  “Article 32. Power of airports authorities

  1. Chief representatives of airports authorities are entitled to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 25,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences if its value is not
  02 times as high as the penalty amount specified in point b of this clause;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.

  2. Directors of airports authorities are entitled to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 50,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.”.

  Article 4. Amendments to Article 33 of the Decree No. 162/2018/ND-CP

  “Article 33. Power of Chairpersons of People’s Committees

  1. Chairpersons of commune-level People’s Committees are entitled to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 50,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.

  2. Chairpersons of provincial People’s Committees are entitled to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 100,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.”.

  Article 5. Amendments to Article 34 of the Decree No. 162/2018/ND-CP

  “Article 34. Power of People’s Public Security

  1. Soldiers of the People’s Public Security in the performance of their duties have the power to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 10,000,000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences if its value is not
  02 times as high as the penalty amount specified in point b of this clause.

  2. Heads of company-level Mobile Police units are entitled to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 20,000,000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences if its value is not
  02 times as high as the penalty amount specified in point b of this clause;

  d) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in points c and d clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.

  3. Heads of Police Posts, Heads of company-level Mobile Police units, Station Heads and Team Leaders are
  entitled to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 30,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences if its value is not
  02 times as high as the penalty amount specified in point b of this clause;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in points c and dd clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.

  4. Commune-level Police Chiefs are entitled to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 50,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.

  5. Heads of Police Offices at International Airports; Heads of professional divisions of the following authorities,
  including Police Department for Administrative Management of Social Order, Traffic Police Department, Fire
  and Rescue Police Department, Immigration Department; Heads of regiment-level Mobile Police units; Heads of
  divisions affiliated to provincial-level Police Departments including heads of investigation police divisions for
  social order crimes, heads of traffic police divisions, heads of mobile police divisions, heads of police divisions
  for investigation into corruption, economy, smuggling and environment-related crimes, heads of fire and rescue
  police divisions, heads of mobile police divisions, Office Chiefs of the Investigation Police Authorities affiliated
  to provincial-level Police Departments are entitled to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 80,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.

  6. Heads of immigration divisions affiliated to provincial-level Police Departments have the power to impose
  penalties as prescribed in clause 5 of this Article.

  7. Directors of provincial-level Police Departments are entitled to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 100,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.

  8. Director General of Police Department for Administrative Management of Social Order, Director General of
  Investigation Police Division for Social Order Crimes, Director General of Traffic Police Department, , Director
  General of Fire and Rescue Police Department, Director General of Environment Crime Prevention and Fighting
  Police Department, Director General of Internal Security Department, Commander of the Mobile Police and
  Office Chief of the Investigation Police Authority affiliated to the Ministry of Public Security are entitled to:

  a) Issue warnings;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 100,000,000;

  c) Suspend the license or suspend the operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or instrumentality involved in commission of administrative offences;

  dd) Enforce the remedial measures mentioned in clause 3 Article 4 of this Decree.

  9. Director General of Immigration Department have the power to impose penalties as prescribed in clause 8 of
  this Article.

  10. The People’s Public Security force has the power to impose penalties for administrative civil aviation
  offences as prescribed in point a clause 1 Article 8; point b clause 4, clause 6 Article 10; points a, b, c clause 1,
  clause 2; points a, b, c, d, dd, l clause 3 Article 11; point a clause 1; point a clause 2, Article 12; Article 14;
  points a, c, e, h clause 4; points a, c, d, dd, e, g clause 5; points a and b clause 6, Article 16, Article 25, Article 26
  and Article 27 of this Decree.”.

  Article 6. Amendments to Article 36 of the Decree No. 162/2018/ND-CP

  “Article 36. Application of other decrees providing for penalty imposition

  1. Persons having the power to impose penalties for administrative civil aviation offences have the power to
  make administrative offence records; impose primary and additional penalties; apply remedial measures to the
  administrative offences mentioned in this Decree and administrative offences that arise in the civil aviation
  sector specified in Decrees providing for impose penalties for administrative offences against regulations on
  prices, charges, fees, invoices; construction activities, production of construction materials, management of
  technical infrastructural constructions, real estate business, housing management and development; security,
  social order and safety; social vice prevention and combat; domestic violence prevention and combat; post,
  telecommunications, radio frequencies, information technology and electronic transactions; commercial
  activities, production and trading of counterfeit and prohibited goods, and protection of consumer rights;
  vocational education and training; environmental protection; water resources and minerals; healthcare.

  2. Principles of determination and distinction of power to impose penalties for administrative offences and apply
  remedial measures shall comply with Article 52 of the Law on Handling of Administrative Violations amended
  by the Law on amendments to some Articles of the Law on Handling of Administrative Violations 2020 and
  2025.”.

  Article 7. Amendments to Article 37 of the Decree No. 162/2018/ND-CP

  “Article 37. Power to make records of administrative offences

  1. The persons having power to make records of administrative civil aviation offences include:

  a) Persons having the power to impose penalties for administrative civil aviation offences, who have the power
  to make records of administrative offences in fields under his/her management, within the scope and contents of
  an inspection or examination;

  b) Members of examination teams upon conducting inspection, who have the power to make records of
  administrative civil aviation offences within the scope and contents of the examination;

  c) Persons of People’s Public Security Forces in the performance of their duties;

  d) Civil servants and public employees of agencies whose heads have the power to impose penalties for
  administrative offences upon conducting inspection, examination, supervision, handling of offences or
  performance of their duties;

  dd) Pilot-in-command, crew members assigned by the pilot-in-command to make records of administrative
  offences which occur on board aircraft in flight bearing Vietnamese nationality.

  2. A pilot-in-command on board an aircraft in flight bearing Vietnamese nationality shall organize the making of
  records of administrative offences which occur on board aircraft in flight.

  The pilot-in-command shall transfer a case of administrative offence committed on board the aircraft to
  competent state management agencies as follows:

  a) The case of offence against regulations on assurance of aviation order and security shall be transferred to the
  aviation security authority at the airport/aerodrome where the aircraft lands;

  b) Another case other than that specified in point a of this clause shall be transferred to the airports authority
  where the aircraft lands.”.

  Article 8. Implementation clause

  1. This Decree comes into force from March 01, 2026 and repeals the following:

  a) Article 35 of the Decree No. 162/2018/ND-CP;

  b) Clauses 20, 21, 22, 23 and 24 Article 3 of the Government’s Decree No. 123/2021/ND-CP dated December
  28, 2021;

  c) Article 67 of the Government’s Decree No. 282/2025/ND-CP dated October 30, 2025.

  2. Ministers, heads of ministerial agencies, heads of Governmental agencies, Chairpersons of People’s
  Committees of provinces and central-affiliated cities, organizations and individuals concerned are responsible for
  the implementation of this Decree.

                                                                                     FOR THE GOVERNMENT
                                                                                     PP. THE PRIME MINISTER
                                                                                   THE DEPUTY PRIME MINISTER

                                                                                                   Tran Hong Ha

