THE GOVERNMENT OF VIETNAM                                SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF VIETNAM
              -------                                         Independence – Freedom – Happiness
                                                                         ----------------
                No. 348/2025/ND-CP                                                       Hanoi, December 30, 2025

                                                       DECREE

   AMENDMENTS TO SOME ARTICLES OF THE GOVERNMENT’S DECREE NO. 45/2019/ND-CP DATED
    MAY 21, 2019 ON PENALTIES FOR ADMINISTRATIVE VIOLATIONS AGAINST REGULATIONS ON
                      TOURISM, AMENDED BY DECREE NO. 129/2021/ND-CP

  Pursuant to the Law on Government Organization No. 63/2025/QH15;

  Pursuant to the Law on Handling of Administrative Violations No. 15/2012/QH13 amended by Law No.
  67/2020/QH14 and Law No. 88/2025/QH15;

  Pursuant to the Law on Tourism No. 09/2017/QH14;

  At the request of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism;

  The Government promulgates Decree on amendments to some articles of the Government’s Decree No.
  45/2019/ND-CP dated May 21, 2019 on penalties for administrative violations against regulations on tourism,
  amended by Decree No. 129/2021/ND-CP.

  Article 1. Annulment of the phrase in Article 6

  The phrase “khoản 7” (clause 7) in clause 8 shall be annulled.

  Article 2. Amendments to and annulment of some points and clauses of Article 7

  1. Point d clause 5 is annulled.

  2. Point c clause 13 is annulled.

  3. Clause 13a shall be added after clause 13 as follows:

   “13a. In case the tour operator lets tourists stay abroad or hide in Vietnam illegally, it shall face the penalty in
  accordance with point d clause 9 Article 21 of the Government’s Decree No. 282/2025/ND-CP dated October 30,
  2025.”

  4. Phrases in some points of clause 15 shall be added or replaced as follows:

  a) The phrase “điểm b và điểm c” (points b and c) shall be added before the phrase “khoản 11" (clause 11) in
  point a.

  b) The phrase “khoản 13” (clause 13) shall be replaced by the phrase “điểm b khoản 13" (point b clause 13) in
  point b.

  c) The phrase “điểm a và điểm b” (points a and b) shall be added before the phrase “khoản 9" (clause 9) in point
  d.

  Article 3. Annulment of phrase and point in Article 9

  1. The phrase “điểm b và” (point b and) in point a clause 10 shall be annulled.

  2. Point b clause 10 shall be annulled.

  Article 4. Replacement of the phrase in Article 10

  The phrase “điểm a và điểm b” (points a and b) shall be replaced by the phrase “điểm a hoặc điểm b" (point a or
  b) in clause 7.

  Article 5. Annulment of clause 5 in Article 12

  Article 6. Amendments to Article 19

  “Article 19. Jurisdiction of Vietnam Maritime Inspectorate

  1. Inspector of Vietnam Maritime Inspectorate has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 5.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 10.000.000.

  2. Chief of inspectorate under Vietnam Maritime Inspectorate has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 25.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  d) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  3. Chief Inspector of Vietnam Maritime Inspectorate has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 40.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.”.

  Article 7. Amendments to Article 20

  “Article 20. Jurisdiction of Chairpersons of People’s Committees

  1. The Chairperson of People’s Committee of commune, ward or special zone (hereinafter referred to as
  "commune-level People’s Committee) has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 25.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  2. The Chairperson of People’s Committee of province or city (hereinafter referred to as "provincial People’s
  Committee) has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 50.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.”.

  Article 8. Amendments to Article 21

  “Article 21. Jurisdiction of market surveillance authorities

  1. On-duty market surveillance official has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 5.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 10.000.000.

  2. Leader of Market Surveillance Team under Sub-Department of Market Surveillance affiliated to Department
  of Industry and Trade has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 15.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 30.000.000.

  d) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  3. Director of Sub-Department of Market Surveillance or Head of Market Surveillance Division under Agency
  for Domestic Market Surveillance and Development has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 25.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  d) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  4. Director of Agency for Domestic Market Surveillance and Development has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 50.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  d) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.”.

  Article 9. Amendments to Article 22

  “Article 22. Jurisdiction of Border Guards

  1. On-duty border guard soldier has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 2.500.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 5.000.000.

  2. Leader of the soldiers specified in clause 1 of this Article has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 5.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 10.000.000.

  3. Leader of Task Force Team for Drug and Crime Prevention and Control under Task Force Commission for
  Drug and Crime Prevention and Control has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 7.500.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 15.000.000.

  4. Captain of Border Guard Station, Leader of Coastal Guard Team, or Commander of Border Guard at Harbor
  Checkpoint has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 15.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 30.000.000;

  d) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  5. Leader of the Drug and Crime Prevention and Control Task Force under the Drug and Crime Prevention
  Department of the Border Guard Command has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 25.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  6. Commanding Officer of Border Guard Command; Captain of Naval Border Guard Squadron, and Director of
  the Drug and Crime Prevention Department affiliated to the Border Guard Command has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 50.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.”.

  Article 10. Amendments to Article 23

  “Article 23. Jurisdiction of Coastguard

  1. On-duty coastguard officer has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 2.500.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 5.000.000.

  2. Leader of coastguard team has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 5.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 10.000.000.

  3. Coastguard squad leader or captain of coastguard station has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 10.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 20.000.000.

  4. Commander of coastguard platoon has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 15.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 30.000.000;

  d) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  5. Captain of Naval Coastguard Squadron; Head of Reconnaissance Commission; Head of Task Force
  Commission for Drug Crime Prevention and Control under the control of the Command of Coast Guard of
  Vietnam has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 25.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  6. Regional Command of Coast Guard or Director of the Department of Operations and Legislation under the
  control of the Command of Coast Guard of Vietnam has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 40.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  7. Commander of Vietnam Coast Guard has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 50.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.”.

  Article 11. Amendments to Article 24

  “Article 24. Jurisdiction of People’s Police Force

  1. On-duty people’s police officer has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 5.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 10.000.000.

  2. Head of company-level Mobile Police Unit has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 10.000.000;

  c) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 20.000.000.

  3. Head of Police Post, Head of Battalion-level Mobile Police Unit, Captain of Squadron, Head of police station
  or Leader of the officers has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 15.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 30.000.000;

  4. Commune-level Police Chief has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 25.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  5. Head of International Airport Police Office; Heads of professional divisions affiliated to Bureau of Homeland
  Security; Heads of professional divisions affiliated to Bureau of Internal Political Security; Heads of professional
  divisions affiliated to Bureau of Economic Security; Heads of professional divisions affiliated to Police Bureau
  for Administrative Management of Social Order; Heads of professional divisions affiliated to Bureau of Traffic
  Police; Heads of professional divisions affiliated to Police Bureau of Fire Prevention and Rescue; Heads of
  professional divisions affiliated to Bureau of Cybersecurity and High-Tech Crime Prevention and Control; Heads
  of professional divisions affiliated to Bureau of Immigration; Heads of Divisions affiliated to the provincial
  Police Authority, including Head of Home Security Division, Head of Internal Political Security Division, Head
  of Police Division for Administrative Management of Social Order, Head of Police Divisions for Investigation
  into Social Order Crimes, Head of Police Division for Investigation into Corruption, Economic, Smuggling and
  Environment Crimes, Head of Police Division for Investigation into Drug-related Crimes, Head of Traffic Police
  Division, Head of Mobile Police Division, Head of Police Division for Execution of Criminal Judgments and
  Judicial Assistance, Head of Police Division for Fire Prevention, Fire Fighting and Rescue, Head of Division of
  Cybersecurity and High-Tech Crime Prevention and Control, Head of Immigration Division, Head of Economic
  Security Division, Head of Foreign Security Division, Chief of Office of the Investigation Police Agency
  affiliated to the provincial Police Authority have the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 40.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  6. Director of the provincial police authority has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 50.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  7. Director of Internal Political Security Bureau, Director of Economic Security Bureau, Chief of the Office of
  the Police Investigation Agency affiliated to the Ministry of Public Security, Director of Police Bureau of
  Administrative Management of Social Order, Director of Police Bureau of Investigation into Social Order-
  related Crimes, Director of Police Bureau of Investigation into Corruption, Economy and Smuggling-related
  Crimes, Director of Police Bureau of Investigation into Drug-related Crimes, Director of Police Traffic Bureau,
  Director of Police Bureau of Fire Prevention and Rescue, Director of Police Bureau of Environmental Crime
  Prevention, Director of Bureau of Cybersecurity and High-Tech Crime Prevention and Control, Director of
  Home Security Bureau, Director of Police Bureau for Managing Custody, Temporary detention and Criminal
  judgment Execution in the Community; Director of Bureau of Immigration; Mobile Police Command, Director
  of the National Data Center has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 50.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.”.

  Article 12. Addition of Article 24a

   “Article 24a. Jurisdiction of Heads of authorities performing state management tasks by fields and
  sectors

  1. Director of Road Management Unit affiliated to Department for Roads of Vietnam; Director of Northern
  Maritime and Waterway Branch; Director of Southern Maritime and Waterway Branch has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 25.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  2. Director of Department of Culture, Sports and Tourism; Director of Department of Tourism; Director of
  Department of Industry and Trade; Director of Department of Construction; Chief of Inspectorate established by
  Director of the Vietnam National Authority of Tourism; Chief of Inspectorate established by Director of
  Department for Roads of Vietnam; and Chief of Inspectorate established by Director of Vietnam Maritime and
  Waterway Administration has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 40.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  3. Director of Vietnam Maritime and Waterway Administration; Director of Department for Roads of Vietnam;
  Director of Department of Environment; Director of Department of Overseas Labour; Director of Vietnam
  National Authority of Tourism; Chief of Office of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism; Chief of
  Inspectorate established by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism; Chief of Inspectorate established by the
  Minister of Construction has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 50.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.”.

  Article 13. Addition of Article 24b

  “Article 24b. Jurisdiction of maritime administration and waterways administration

  1. Chief representative of maritime administration or waterways administration has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 12.500.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation if its value does not exceed
  VND 25.000.000;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.

  2. Director of maritime administration or waterways administration has the jurisdiction to:

  a) Issue warning;

  b) Impose a fine of up to VND 25.000.000;

  c) Suspend license or practicing certificate or operation for a fixed period;

  d) Confiscate any exhibit or mean used for commission of administrative violation;

  dd) Implement remedial measures specified in Article 4 of this Decree.”.

  Article 14. Amendments to Article 25

  “Article 25. Determination of jurisdiction to impose penalties for administrative violations against
  regulations on tourism

  1. Chairpersons of People’s Committees at all levels have the jurisdiction to make administrative violation
  records, and impose administrative penalties and remedial measures on administrative violations prescribed in
  Chapter II of this Decree.

  2. Directors of Departments of Culture, Sports and Tourism and Departments of Tourism; Chief of Inspectorate
  established by Director of the Vietnam National Authority of Tourism; Director of the Vietnam National
  Authority of Tourism; Chief of Office of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism; Chief of Inspectorate
  established by the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism have the jurisdiction to impose penalties for
  administrative violations specified in Chapter II of this Decree; point d clause 9 Article 21 of the Decree No.
  282/2025/ND-CP and point c clause 2 Article 52 the Government’s Decree No. 122/2021/ND-CP dated
  December 28, 2021.

  3. Director of Road Management Unit affiliated to Department for Roads of Vietnam; Director of Northern
  Maritime and Waterway Branch; Director of Southern Maritime and Waterway Branch; Director of maritime
  administration or waterways administration; Director of Department of Construction; Chief of Inspectorate
  established by Director of Department for Roads of Vietnam; Chief of Inspectorate established by Director of
  Vietnam Maritime and Waterway Administration; Vietnam Maritime Inspectorate; Director of Vietnam Maritime
  and Waterway Administration; Director of Department for Roads of Vietnam; Chief of Inspectorate established
  by the Minister of Construction have the jurisdiction to impose penalties for administrative violations specified
  in Articles 17 and 18 of this Decree.

  4. Director of Department of Overseas Labour has the jurisdiction to impose penalties for administrative
  violations specified in point a clause 5, point d clause 13 Article 7; failure to reach employment agreements with
  tour operators or tour guide service providers as prescribed point d clause 5, clause 9 Article 9 of this Decree.

  5. Director of Department of Environment has the jurisdiction to impose penalties for administrative violations
  specified in clause 4 Article 11; point a, clause 5 Article 13; point e clause 3, points g, h and i clause 4; point b
  clause 5 Article 16 of this Decree.

  6. Directors of Department of Industry and Trade and market surveillance authorities have the jurisdiction to
  impose penalties for administrative violations specified in point a clause 3, point c clause 4 Article 6; point b
  clause 3 Article 8; point c clause 1, clause 4 Article 10; clause 1, point h clause 4 Article 13 of this Decree.

  7. Border Guards have the jurisdiction to impose penalties for administrative violations specified in point a
  clause 3, point c clause 4, clauses 5, 6 and 7 Article 6; clause 1, point dd clause 2, clause 4, point a clause 5,
  point c clause 7, point b clause 8, points a and c clause 9, clause 10 and clause 13a Article 7; clauses 1, 2, 3, 4
  and 5, points b and c clause 6, clauses 7, 8 and 9 Article 9; Article 14; clauses 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 7 Article 15;
  Articles 17 and 18 of this Decree.

  8. Coastguard has the jurisdiction to impose penalties for administrative violations specified in clauses 5, 6 and 7
  Article 6; clauses 1 and 4 Article 7; Article 9; Article 14; clauses 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 7 Article 15; Article 17; Article
  18 of this Decree.

  9. People’s Police Force has the jurisdiction to impose penalties for administrative violations specified in points
  a and b of clause 3, points a and c of clause 4, clauses 5, 6 and 7 of Article 6; clause 1, points b and c of clause 2,
  points a and c of clause 4, point c of clause 8, points b, c and d of clause 9, point d of clause 13, clause 13a, point
  dd of clause 14 of Article 7; clauses 6 and 7 of Article 8; clauses 3 and 4, points a and b of clause 6, clauses 7, 8
  and 9 of Article 9; clause 6 of Article 10; clause 4 of Article 12; point b of clause 5 of Article 13; Article 14;
  Clauses 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 and 8 of Article 15; clause 1, point a of clause 2, point c of clause 3, points k and l of
  clause 4, point a of clause 5 of Article 16 and Article 17 of this Decree.”.

  Article 15. Amendments to clauses 1 and 2 Article 26

  “1. Persons having the jurisdiction to impose penalties for administrative violations specified in Article 19 thru
  Article 24b of this Decree may make violation records in conformity with their functions, tasks and powers as
  assigned in Article 25 of this Decree.

  2. Civil servants and employees assigned to conduct inspections in the tourism field may make administrative
  violation records and transfer administrative violation dossiers to persons having the jurisdiction to impose
  penalties to impose penalties in accordance with the law.”

  Article 16. Implementation clauses

  This Decree takes effect from the date February 15, 2026.

  Article 17. Transition clauses

  In case administrative violation dossiers are being processed, decisions to impose administrative penalties have
  been issued or have been completely executed before the effective date of this Decree but organizations and
  individuals incurring such penalties lodge complaints, regulations of the Government’s Decree No. 45/2019/ND-
  CP dated May 21, 2019; the Government's Decree No. 129/2021/ND-CP dated December 30, 2021 shall apply.

                                                                          ON BEHALF OF THE GOVERNMENT
                                                                                PP. PRIME MINISTER
                                                                              DEPUTY PRIME MINISTER

                                                                                              Mai Van Chinh

